<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Godelete - Tag - loommii</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/godelete/</link><description>我的个人技术博客</description><generator>Hugo 0.165.0 &amp; FixIt v0.4.5</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 16 Jan 2026 01:28:43 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/godelete/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Go Daily Question 142</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_142/</link><pubDate>Wed, 25 Dec 2024 00:24:33 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_142/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#10;&#10;import &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#10;&#10;func main() {&#10; var s map[string]int&#10; delete(s, &amp;#34;h&amp;#34;)&#10; fmt.Println(s[&amp;#34;h&amp;#34;])&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;A. runtime panic&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;B. 0&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;C. compilation error&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;B&#10;&lt;a href="https://go.dev/play/p/rfK0pIKBRRx" target="_blank" rel="external nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Using &lt;code&gt;delete&lt;/code&gt; on an uninitialized map (not made with &lt;code&gt;make&lt;/code&gt;) will not cause an error.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Accessing an uninitialized map returns the zero value corresponding to the value type.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;h4 class="heading-element" id="extension"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Extension&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="#extension" class="heading-mark"&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;Assigning to an uninitialized map will cause a panic.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 141</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_141/</link><pubDate>Wed, 25 Dec 2024 00:09:11 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_141/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() {&#10; s := make(map[string]int)&#10; delete(s, &amp;#34;h&amp;#34;)&#10; fmt.Println(s[&amp;#34;h&amp;#34;])&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;A. runtime panic&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;B. 0&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;C. compilation error&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;B&#10;&lt;a href="https://go.dev/play/p/uvHvPF8EdU-" target="_blank" rel="external nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&#10;Deleting a non-existent key does not cause a panic.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h4 class="heading-element" id="extended-question"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Extended Question&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="#extended-question" class="heading-mark"&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;In this problem, &lt;code&gt;s&lt;/code&gt; is already initialized. Would the behavior be the same if it were uninitialized?&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 105</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_105/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 23:42:44 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_105/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output value of &lt;code&gt;counter&lt;/code&gt; in the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() {&#10; var m = map[string]int{&#10; &amp;#34;A&amp;#34;: 21,&#10; &amp;#34;B&amp;#34;: 22,&#10; &amp;#34;C&amp;#34;: 23,&#10; }&#10; counter := 0&#10; for k, v := range m {&#10; if counter == 0 {&#10; delete(m, &amp;#34;A&amp;#34;)&#10; }&#10; counter&amp;#43;&amp;#43;&#10; fmt.Println(k, v)&#10; }&#10; fmt.Println(&amp;#34;counter is &amp;#34;, counter)&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;A. 2&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;B. 3&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;C. 2 or 3&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;C&#10;Maps are reference types and will affect the original map.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 050</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_050/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:44:29 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_050/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() { &#10; s := make(map[string]int)&#10; delete(s, &amp;#34;h&amp;#34;)&#10; fmt.Println(s[&amp;#34;h&amp;#34;])&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;A. runtime panic&#10;B. 0&#10;C. compilation error&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;B 0&#10;Deleting a non-existent key will not cause a panic.&#10;Outputting a non-existent key will return the zero value of its type.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Extension:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() {&#10; var s map[string]int&#10; delete(s, &amp;#34;h&amp;#34;)&#10; s[&amp;#34;h&amp;#34;] = 1&#10; fmt.Println(s[&amp;#34;h&amp;#34;])&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;Deleting from a nil map will also not panic.&#10;However, writing to a nil map will panic.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>